    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0733" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1947v04/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/12–2047</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé of the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tsarapkin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State for Economic
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thorp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 250</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-20">December 20,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Acknowledging receipt of your letter of December 11, 1947, concerning eight
                    lend-lease vessels, I hereby inform you that the Government of the Union of
                    Soviet Socialist Republics considers that this question is subject to decision
                    in the course of the general lend-lease settlement, concerning which concrete
                    proposals were presented by the Soviet side to the American side on December 16,
                    1947.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsarapkin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
